.Pp
Compile
.Ar script
without running it and report every error.
With no
.Ar script ,
check standard input instead.
The exit status is 0 after errors are reported,
unless
.Fl b
is given.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl e ,
.Fl "-lint-error"
.Ar level
.Xc
Set the lint level at which a message stops compilation with
an error.
.Ar level
is one of
.Ql "none" ,
.Ql "relaxed" ,
.Ql "normal" ,
.Ql "strict"
or
.Ql "all" ,
written without a leading colon,
or a number.
These are the numbers 0,
1,
2 and 3 and infinity.
A message is reported when its own level is at most
.Ar level ,
so
.Ql "none"
reports nothing and
.Ql "all"
reports every message.
The default is
.Ql "none" .
.It Xo
.Fl w ,
.Fl "-lint-warn"
.Ar level
.Xc
Set the lint level at which a message is printed as a warning.
.Ar level
takes the same values as for
.Fl e .
The default is
.Ql "normal" .
.It Xo
.Fl b ,
.Fl "-bail"
.Xc
Stop at the first error in the source and exit with status 1.
.El
