.Ss run
.Nm
.Oo
.Fl s
.Ar path
.Oc
[\c
.Ic run ]
.Oo
.Ar options
.Oc
.Oo
.Ar script
.Oo
.Ar args
.No ...
.Oc
.Oc
.Pp
Options are read until the first argument that does not begin
with
.Ql "-" .
That argument is the
.Ar script ,
and every argument after it is passed to the script without
being read as an option.
Once the script has run,
.Nm
calls the
.Ql "main"
function it defines,
if any,
with the script’s path followed by
.Ar args .
The same list is bound to
.Ql "*args*" .
With no
.Ar script ,
and no
.Fl e ,
.Ic run
starts a REPL.
.Pp
An error that a
.Ar script ,
a module loaded with
.Fl l
or code given to
.Fl e
does not handle ends the process with status 1.
.Pp
The options are applied in a fixed order,
whatever order they are written in:
first the settings (\c
.Fl d ,
.Fl s ,
.Fl r ,
.Fl q
and
.Fl i ) ,
then
.Fl l ,
then
.Fl e ,
and last the
.Ar script .
A setting therefore applies to every library,
expression and script,
and
.Fl l
runs before every
.Fl e .
Several
.Fl e
options and several
.Fl l
options run in the order given.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl e ,
.Fl "-eval"
.Ar code
.Xc
Evaluate
.Ar code
as Wattle source.
The REPL is not started afterwards unless
.Fl r
is also given.
.It Xo
.Fl l ,
.Fl "-lib"
.Ar module
.Xc
Import
.Ar module
into the environment before continuing,
without a prefix,
so its bindings are available to later options,
the
.Ar script
and the REPL.
.It Xo
.Fl i ,
.Fl "-img"
.Xc
Treat
.Ar script
as an image made by
.Ic build img
rather than as source,
load it and call its
.Ql "main"
function.
.It Xo
.Fl r ,
.Fl "-repl"
.Xc
Start the REPL after the
.Ar script
or the other options have run.
.It Xo
.Fl s ,
.Fl "-stdin"
.Xc
Read REPL input as raw lines from standard input and write prompts
to standard output.
Implies
.Fl r .
.It Xo
.Fl d ,
.Fl "-debug"
.Xc
Set
.Ql "*debug*"
and
.Ql "*redef*" .
An error in the REPL enters the debugger,
and a top-level definition can be rebound.
.It Xo
.Fl q ,
.Fl "-quiet"
.Xc
Do not print the banner when the REPL starts.
.El
.
.Ss test
.Nm
.Oo
.Fl s
.Ar path
.Oc
.Ic test
.Oo
.Ar options
.Oc
.Pp
Run the tests.
.Ic test
runs each file ending in
.Ql "\&.wattle"
under
.Ql "\&./test" ,
in a process of its own.
It prints
.Ql "seed:"
and the seed.
It then prints one line for each file,
with a mark,
the path and the counts of tests and assertions.
It prints the output of a file that failed after its line,
each line after a border that is red when colour is on.
It ends with the number of files and tests and the files that
failed.
The output of a file that passed is not printed.
The exit status is 1 if a file failed or no file was run.
A test file that uses the Gum test module,
.Ql "gum/test\&.wattle" ,
reads the dynamic bindings that
.Fl t ,
.Fl T
and
.Fl "-seed"
set.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl f ,
.Fl "-file"
.Ar path
.Xc
Run only the test file whose path ends with
.Ar path ,
which is relative to
.Ql "\&./test" .
It can be repeated.
It is not compatible with
.Fl F .
.It Xo
.Fl F ,
.Fl "-no-file"
.Ar path
.Xc
Do not run the test file whose path ends with
.Ar path .
It can be repeated.
It is not compatible with
.Fl f .
.It Xo
.Fl t ,
.Fl "-test"
.Ar name
.Xc
Add
.Ar name
to the dynamic binding
.Ql ":test/tests"
in each test file.
It can be repeated.
It is not compatible with
.Fl T .
.It Xo
.Fl T ,
.Fl "-no-test"
.Ar name
.Xc
Add
.Ar name
to the dynamic binding
.Ql ":test/skips"
in each test file.
It can be repeated.
It is not compatible with
.Fl t .
.It Xo
.Fl "-seed"
.Ar seed
.Xc
Use the integer
.Ar seed
to seed the generator that shuffles the test files.
Each test file also shuffles its tests with it,
as
.Ic test
sets the dynamic binding
.Ql ":test/seed" .
Without
.Fl "-seed" ,
the seed is taken from the clock,
so each run has a different order.
The same seed gives the same order.
.It Xo
.Fl b ,
.Fl "-bail"
.Xc
Stop after the first test file that fails.
.It Xo
.Fl e ,
.Fl "-lint-error"
.Ar level ,
.Fl w ,
.Fl "-lint-warn"
.Ar level
.Xc
Set the lint levels of each test file.
They take the same values as for
.Ic check .
.El
